# Mobile UI (iOS & Android)

**Canonical folder:** `lib/mobile/`. Targets: `ios/`, `android/` runners only.

## Structure

```
lib/mobile/
  design/       # mobile-only layout tokens (optional; extend lib/design/app_tokens.dart)
  layout/       # safe areas, tab insets, phone/tablet breakpoints
  screens/      # full mobile screens and *Body widgets
  widgets/
    shell/      # MainShellScaffold, LiquidGlassNavBar, auth layout
    catalog/    # browse panels, book tiles, strips
    reader/     # mobile reader chrome
```

## Conventions

- Touch-first: `Scaffold`, `SafeArea`, `RefreshIndicator`, bottom nav — no sidebar.
- Shell: `LiquidGlassNavBar` tabs (Home, Settings, Profile).
- Auth: `AuthScreenLayout` in `mobile/widgets/shell/` (not `WebAuthLayout`).
- Primitives: `AppPanel`, `AppListRow`, `AppGreetingCard` — one greeting card per shell screen max.
- Catalog: expansion cards, vertical lists — not web grids/hover cards.
- All strings via `AppLocalizations`.

## Do / don't

```dart
// ✅ Mobile widget in lib/mobile/
import '../../providers/catalog_providers.dart';  // common
import '../../design/app_tokens.dart';           // common

// ❌ Never import web or desktop UI
import '../../web/widgets/shell/web_sidebar.dart';
import '../../desktop/widgets/shell/desktop_sidebar.dart';
```

- Touch targets ≥ 48dp; `BouncingScrollPhysics` on lists.
- Platform APIs (secure storage, `FLAG_SECURE`) stay in common `storage/` / utils — not duplicated in widgets.

## Legacy paths

`lib/widgets/` and mobile branches in `lib/screens/` are **legacy**. When editing, prefer adding/moving code to `lib/mobile/`. Route adapters stay in `lib/screens/`.
